From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:30:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] BD-J host: a disc cannot fill the player's log

What the disc's Java does can make the player's process write lines without end, and a player
such as Kodi writes these lines to its log without debug logging (they say why the Java of a disc
does not run). Each kind now has a cap for the connection to the BD-J host, that is, for a disc:

- the names of BD-Live: the first BDR_NET_LOG_LINES (100) lines; past them a notice, once a
  minute how many were left out, and the count at the end. The limits on lookups (4 at once, 20
  a second) held back getaddrinfo(), not the log: 20000 requests gave 19996 lines in 2 ms
  (review3a); now 101 while asked, and the count at the end. The same with BD-Live off: the
  client now always has its BDR_NET, which refuses every name then, within the same cap;
- the lines of the host: at most 100 a second as before, and now 2000 in all (LOG_LINES_TOTAL);
  past them a notice, once a minute how many, and the count at the end;
- the requests of the host the client refuses, which it may repeat (a path that is not one or
  leads out of the disc, a drawing outside its plane): the first 100 lines, and the count at the
  end. A refused path is shown without its control characters: it comes from the disc.
